lding a bomb is significant. Additionally, the opponent still has 15 cards, so there is no immediate threat of them finishing. My hand contains several small singles (6, 8) that need to be cleared; keeping the Rocket allows me to regain initiative at a more critical juncture or punish a bomb play. Wasting a Joker or the Rocket on a single 2 provides little value compared to the security and potential score doubling the Rocket offers.\n\nReason: To preserve the Rocket for critical defense against potential bombs (indicated by the missing Jacks and 7s) and to maintain the highest control for later in the game. Beating a single 2 with a Joker is an inefficient use of resources when the opponent has a large hand size remaining.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": []}'}
