ng, which is high. Using a 2 to beat it would break my pair of 2s, weakening my defense against pair leads, and forces me to take the lead while I still have several isolated singles (6, 8, Q) that are difficult to lead with. By passing, I allow the Left player (who has 16 cards and will likely lead small cards to communicate or offload) to play a new hand. This gives me a better opportunity to dispose of my small singles (6, 8) or use my pairs effectively, while reserving my 2s and Rocket for critical moments or to catch the Right player (who has 8 cards) if they try to finish.\n\nReason: Beating a King with a 2 is inefficient when holding a hand with multiple mid-rank singles that need to be cleared. Preserving the pair of 2s and the Rocket ensures I can handle any threat later, while passing gives a chance for a lower lead that suits my hand better.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": []}'}
