e Ace is unaccounted for). This would weaken my hand structure significantly, leaving me with loose high singles and unable to defend against pair runs effectively. Since I have 9 cards including weak singles (6, 8) and a mid-pair (99), I should not rush to take the lead with an expensive card. Passing puts the pressure on the Next Player (Right) to beat the Queen, potentially forcing them to use a high card like a King or Ace, or allows the Previous Player (Left) to lead again, which is acceptable given they have 15 cards. I retain the Rocket as an ultimate defense.\n\nReason: Beating a single Queen with a 2 or Joker is an over-commitment of resources ("waste") given my current hand structure and the lack of immediate threat from the opponents. Preserving the pair of 2s is strategically better for controlling the game later.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": []}'}
