nce no high pairs exist, it makes a very strong lead. This move also lets me to utilize my remaining singles.\n\nThe data supports playing the pair 99, and I get JSON format:\n\n{"cards": ["♠9", "♣9"]}\n\n\n', 'output': 'Evaluation: You possess a strong hand with the Rocket (Red & Black Joker) and the 2, ensuring you can regain control at least twice. Analyzing the remaining unknown cards, there is only 1 card left for each rank of 10, Q, K, A, and 2. This means **it is impossible for any opponent to have a pair higher than your 99**, except for a pair of Jacks (since there are 4 Jacks left). This makes your pair of 9s effectively the second-highest pair possible in the current game state.\n\nReason: Playing the pair of 9s (♠9 ♣9) is the optimal strategy. Since opponents likely lack high pairs (except potentially Jacks), this move has a very high chance of going unanswered, allowing you to maintain the initiative (the "lead"). If you play a single like the 6, the Next Player (who has only 7 cards) could easily beat it with a 10 or similar to shed cards. Playing 99 applies maximum pressure and clears your only pair, leaving you with singles that can be protected by your 2 and Rocket.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♠9", "♣9"]}'}
