b (Quad Jacks possible), maintaining the Rocket is crucial for defense and regaining the lead. After winning with the 2, I can play my lowest card (8). If the opponents beat it, I can use the Rocket to secure the lead again and play my final card (Queen) to win. This strategy offers a guaranteed win path assuming no higher bomb counters the Rocket (which is impossible as Rocket is the highest). Passing is dangerous as the opponent has only 6 cards and could play a combination I cannot block.\n\nReason: The ♣2 is the strongest single card available to win the lead immediately. It keeps the Rocket intact, which is essential to counter any potential bombs from the opponents or to override their high cards when clearing my small cards (8 and Q). This sequence maximizes the chance of emptying my hand first.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♣2"]}'}
